==Latin==

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*wekʷ-}}
From {{der|la|itc-pro|*wōks}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*wṓkʷs||speech, voice}} (with stem ''vōc-'' for ''voqu-'' from the nominative case), an [[o-grade]] [[root noun]] of {{m|ine-pro|*wekʷ-||to speak}}. Cognates include {{cog|sa|sc=Deva|वाच्|tr=vā́c}}, {{cog|grc|ὄψ}}, and {{cog|sq|ves}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|eccl=yes|vōx}}
* {{audio|la|la-cls-vox.ogg|Audio (Classical)}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|vōx<3>|g=f}}

# [[voice]]
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Caesar|Caesar]]|[[w:de Bello Gallico|de Bello Gallico]]|VII, 17|quote=Nulla tamen '''vox''' est ab eis audita|t=Although no '''voice''' was heard from them}}
